WEBVTT

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.600
The sound is just slightly impure.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.000
But this piano should be perfectly tuned.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.170
This is your new classmate.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.360
I'm Akbarjin Batbayar.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.680
Nice to meet you.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:44.560
Mr. Akba... Akbarjin scored excellently in the Meso-Asiatic training program.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:48.400
He is an Element candidate, and we expect him to be a reserve pilot.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.400
Be nice to him.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.120
Is he from there?

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.240
I hope he'll pull his weight.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.910
A-Are these...

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.160
real live...

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.410
Rare Iguras?

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.160
You think he likes holes? I hope so!

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.960
I guess.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.940
Huh. He's pretty cute.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.920
He's a bottom. I'm sure of it.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.360
Wait. What if he's a top and just looks like a bottom?

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.800
Ooh!

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.560
It's just a new boy. Don't lose your head over it.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.270
What are you staring at?

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.000
Are you interested in boys like him?

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.760
That's not it. I just remembered...

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.060
I was a transfer student, too.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:13.920
Were there girls at your training site, too?

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.380
Oh, cut it out. You can look that up.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.040
So, what kind of music do you listen to?

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.800
What's with him?

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:27.890
What a creep.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.920
What am I supposed to do?

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.240
I have to observe.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.940
Have you checked out the school?

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.080
We'll show you around if you want.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.170
Observe... Observe...

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:54.960
Observe...

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.170
Ew!

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.920
I'll show you around the school.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:06.930
Follow me.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.120
That's the Berlin.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:17.200
For a long time, the wall separated Neo-Deava Academy into two areas based on gender.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.070
But part of the wall was broken—

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:24.060
Can you at least look? I'm trying to tell you something.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.490
Can you even see? Your hair's covering your eyes.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:29.040
Don't touch me!

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.280
I can see just fine.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.260
This place is the center of Neo-Deava.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.020
Here, we store all the data on the Elements' powers,

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.720
and direct Aquarion's strategies and tactics.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.720
What's Aquarion?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.740
Look as much as you wish.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:10.330
If you bear no insincerity, you will see things as they truly are.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.920
What's that "Aquarion" you mentioned?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.500
You don't know? I thought you passed training.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.540
It's the new name for the Aquaria.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.560
The Machine Angel?

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.100
That's Aquarion right there.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:34.390
If you're going to be a guide, you have to be nice.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.020
I <i>am</i> being nice.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.680
So nice that I want to puke.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.000
Shut it!

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.860
Hey, no need to get violent!

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.220
You think that's enough to provoke me?

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.860
You grabbed me by the collar when you were my guide!

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.240
That's because you were making a move on Mikono!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.900
No, I wasn't! Well, back then, I—

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:56.120
Back then? So you are now?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.040
That's not what I meant!

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:00.380
Hey...

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:03.700
Where did that kid go?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.760
A hangar?

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.180
So those machines form the Machine Angel.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.880
Steal the Machine Angel?

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.720
You don't have to bring back the whole thing.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:26.290
At least get us one of the component machines.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.460
This might be a little over my head.

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:30.850
Only do it if you can.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:35.300
Your top priority is to investigate Rare Iguras that could serve as the true Eve.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:40.000
We're celebrating the news of your survival.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.580
Finish your mission and get back as soon as you can.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.470
You could just come and get me if you're so worried.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.860
What?

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:50.200
Nothing.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.320
Just establish yourself in Neo-Deava.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.470
We'll talk more after that.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:59.320
Understood. I'll do it.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:07.700
It may be Alicia's birthplace, but I don't plan to stay here forever.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:17.120
A computer terminal in the dead of night.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:20.240
My program connected to the internet.

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:26.460
It was so simple to overwrite the history file of a student who was supposed to transfer in.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:32.420
I'll find the most powerful Rare Igura soon enough.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.020
Yeah, that's right. Get out of my way.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.260
That way, I can investigate without being bothered.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.180
But why a re you digging here?

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.540
Because this spot is begging me to dig!

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.290
I won't let anybody stop me!

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.740
Jeez...

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.920
Hey! My arms are stuck!

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.560
That's your punishment for disobeying me.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.850
That's a Rare Igura?

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.580
Don't you think discipline around here is slipping a little lately?

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:29.230
I don't know what you mean by that.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.240
I wish you'd take this seriously!

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:36.740
That stuff's going to happen if you take the wall away.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:42.870
You of all people should be most worried about the Elements falling in love.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.280
In that case, let's just never approve a Union again.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.380
We can't lose sight of our actual goals.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.510
But!

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:51.200
You'll get wrinkles that way.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:55.470
I'm trying to be serious!

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:59.420
Ah! No!

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:02.520
I can't believe it! Rare Iguras are really dangerous!

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.080
Come on! Faster!

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:07.610
Melon bread for a limited time only!

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:08.620
I'll take one!

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:09.820
Me, too!

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:10.610
I had that one first!

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:23.000
Rare Iguras... Women...

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:26.810
These ones aren't like Silvie at all!

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:27.920
Who's there?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.860
He's trying to peep on us! Get him out of here!

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:35.840
The new kid? No way!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.160
Really?

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:38.300
What a creep.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.640
Don't let him escape! Lock the doors!

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:44.980
So what brings you here?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.700
Bet he was trying to see us naked.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.860
Crucify him!

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:50.400
Excuse me...

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:55.380
I don't think he did it on purpose.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:59.260
I got lost a lot back when I first came here.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.800
One time, I wandered into the boys' bathroom...

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.580
I'm so embarrassed!

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:06.620
Who is that?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.440
Is that right?

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:12.710
You didn't know this was the girls' locker room?

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.240
That's right!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.710
I got lost! Honest!

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:17.340
It's the truth!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.540
Yo. We've been waiting for you, Akb... umm...

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:28.500
Something-jin.

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:32.980
Hey, Ak... Ack... What was it?

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.980
Can we just call you Jin?

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:38.530
My name's Andy. Nice to meet ya.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:49.830
Hey!

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:54.840
Jin? Seriously?

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.130
Hey bro, do you like holes?

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:00.510
Holes?

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.140
Yep! Holes!

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:09.770
Can't I get any peace?

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:13.040
Do they not know what privacy means on this planet?

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:23.280
So he was like, "Man, it's really bad!"

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:26.200
And I was like, "How bad?" And he was like, "So bad that I don't even know!"

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:31.220
I know, right? You wait the whole
time and never actually get anywhere.

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:33.480
It's awful! I can't take it!

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:37.790
Is this some kind of code? How can they understand each other?

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:40.100
Perhaps I'll never understand Rare Iguras.

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:49.400
Is anyone sitting here?

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:50.100
No.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.480
Mikono! And Amata!

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.360
You looked like you were about to vanish.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.260
I'm all right now.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.280
Is something the matter?

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:05.270
I've been wanting to tell you this, but...

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:07.620
I'm really sorry for what I did!

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.920
That's ancient history now.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.090
Yeah, Mikono just totally misunderstood.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.550
Are you saying that it's my fault?

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:23.220
No! Sorry!

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.640
Oh, Amata...

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.980
I suppose I did...

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:32.040
You think so?

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:33.270
Maybe...

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.480
Hey, Jin!

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:40.400
Jin?

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:45.200
His name's really hard to say, so Andy started calling him Jin.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.140
I guess he's not very good with people.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.360
I'm really worried about him!

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.860
N-Not like that.

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:57.300
I remember when I was like him.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:57.940
Huh?

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:03.170
I didn't always know how to disappear.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:08.760
When I came here, everyone wanted to talk to me,

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:13.430
but I was too shy to have a conversation.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:18.610
I ended up all alone.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.360
I felt like no one could even see me.

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:29.300
Then I thought that it would be nice...

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.490
if no one really could see me.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.540
I felt like that all the time.

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:37.000
And so...

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:44.660
So that's how it happened.

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.930
It was all my fault.

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:51.280
They were just trying to be nice to me.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:53.520
But I didn't even try to respond.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.620
I'm worried that Jin might be the same.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:00.020
It's the girl from the locker room!

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:05.720
What's troubling you, my friend?

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:12.950
Look who's asking. You don't come out very often.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:16.880
You're not looking well. Did you have another nightmare?

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.460
The wedding in mourning clothes again?

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.210
A one-eyed giant.

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.960
A one-eyed giant?

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.640
What could it mean?

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:34.280
If I knew, it wouldn't be bothering me so much.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:37.890
So what do you want to ask me?

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.060
There's a noise I'm curious about.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:43.460
I wanted to let you know.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:45.340
What noise?

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:49.680
A little noise that came to school a few days ago.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:54.960
It might have to do with that vanished Abductor that you've been chasing.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:56.410
A few days ago?

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:08.130
I don't understand this!

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.890
Looking at these isn't helping.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:16.180
Rare Iguras truly are a mystery.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.190
Ow!

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.360
I'm sorry!

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:32.320
That's mine!

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:33.920
Oh, Jin!

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.020
She disappeared!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.200
Here you go.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.820
Thank you.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:47.520
Is your device still working?

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:48.840
What do you mean?

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:51.880
I'm sorry.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.550
I don't think it's wrong, though.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.680
Anyway, you really surprised me.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.800
You have the power to just disappear.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:15:59.900
That's fantastic!

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:00.930
It is?

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.860
You can be alone whenever you want!

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.760
I suppose...

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:07.560
I think that would be awesome!

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:10.070
No one would ever bother you!

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:13.900
I don't think it's good to be alone.

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:15.170
Why?

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:17.490
"Why?" Well, I'd get lonely.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.260
But it'd be so much nicer!

00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:22.310
It's not right. It's just not.

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:24.000
All those other people reached out...

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:27.670
I had so many chances to make friends with them...

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:31.510
So why... why did I...

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:41.350
I'm embarrassed!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:56.990
A noise that came to the school a few days ago.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:59.160
And a one-eyed giant.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:05.400
If he's the giant... the Abductor's pilot...

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.380
Mix.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:14.980
Element power: Spatial augmentation.

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:17.240
So basically, filling holes?

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:19.140
Element index 112.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:22.100
Aura level increase pattern A.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:25.640
Hey, Jin! Wanna go out and dig holes with us?

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:28.280
Hey, it won't open.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:30.520
These things do have locks, you know.

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:32.840
Digging holes? Give me a break.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.760
Yunoha?

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:37.440
Yunoha Thrul.

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:40.330
Element power: Optical fluoroscopy.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:55.800
I looked over your data.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.590
Well done.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:17:58.590
Thanks.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.940
So far, the data is consistent with our predictions.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:06.500
There's a high probability that one of these Rare Iguras

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:10.110
has the right qualities to be the True Eve.

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:13.920
But Rare Iguras are not to be taken lightly.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:17.150
They look perfectly harmless, but they can make men dance in the palms of their hands.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:20.570
And they have a very powerful weapon.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.530
A weapon? What is it?

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:24.800
Tears.

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:26.230
Tears?

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.600
Did something happen to you?

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:32.960
I... the one who shot me down... and...

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.540
You were defeated again?

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.840
Not exactly.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:40.760
If you find a dangerous Rare Igura, bring her back.

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:41.680
What?

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:48.400
Our goal is to obtain a Rare Igura who can be the True Eve.

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:54.270
You want to dig a hole?

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:57.320
Yes! You finally came around!

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:00.560
You might not want to. It's pretty intense.

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:03.990
Jealous, Amata? You want to dig with just me?

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.010
Jealous?

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:07.470
Right!

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:09.520
We are now the three digging bros!

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:12.130
Why did I come?

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:24.300
Nice! Good job!

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:29.000
Behold, Jin, the new world we have blazed a trail into.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.620
The forbidden girls' dorms!

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:35.270
Amata! You're holding us back!

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:40.480
Where have you been? Jin's already—

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:44.090
Where'd he go?

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:44.660
Dunno.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.660
Jin! Where are you!

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:52.870
Don't yell so loud, or they'll find the hole.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:55.630
You're worried about the hole?

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.480
So that's Yunoha's room.

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:09.620
She's the Rare Igura who defeated me...

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.240
Jin!

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:28.740
Um, I... can we continue that conservation we had earlier?

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:32.300
About it being wrong to be alone?

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:40.160
Oh no! What should I do?

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:43.900
But Jin wants to hear what I have to say.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:46.760
Does that mean he's ready to make friends?

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:49.680
I guess that's a no.

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:51.300
I won't take that!

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.380
Did you hear that?

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:14.370
That was a stun ray gun!

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:16.880
What do you intend to do to Yunoha?

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:19.960
I'm not doing anything to her.

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:21.760
I just want to talk.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.440
Stop lying!

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:26.400
Why did you really come to Neo-Deava?

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:27.700
Stop, Cayenne!

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:31.940
Let me go! I'm not going to kill him!

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:33.890
Of course not!

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:35.850
Not so fast!

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:38.310
Don't do it! Jin hasn't done anything!

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:43.760
Yunoha!

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:53.450
Was that a barrier? Did he stop it with a barrier?

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:57.170
Is that his Element power?

00:21:58.070 --> 00:22:02.180
Did... Did I do that?

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:19.760
The noise has not disappeared.

00:22:20.550 --> 00:22:23.690
But perhaps it's beginning to get clearer.

00:22:27.090 --> 00:22:29.320
The power to isolate.

00:22:30.090 --> 00:22:35.440
But there will be things in life you cannot wall yourself away from.

00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:39.100
What will you do then, boy?

00:24:10.850 --> 00:24:11.800
Why?

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:15.180
Why does my heart race when I think of her?

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:20.980
This is just like when Alicia was wearing white bloomers in her new downloadable music video!

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:24.400
Next time on Aquarion Evol: Call of the Wild.
